  "rubric_items": {
    "anchors_resolve": "pass \u2014 `reckon crew host` resolves to `crew_follow_commands.py:3241`; the station's live-work reading resolves to `station_subscriber.py`; the test files named are new deliverables, so they cite nothing that must already exist; no extensionless hrefs are used in these units.",
    "done_when": "a finding \u2014 both negative controls say only \"at the base revision\", with no revision fixed, where s103\u2013s108 each pin theirs as \"main after <sha>\"; the arm the control rests on is not reproducible.",
    "evidence_paths": "a finding \u2014 neither section's done-when names an arm log path, gate command or closing `EXIT=` line, where \u00a7116 and \u00a7114 in this same plan carry exactly that discipline.",
    "naming": "pass \u2014 test file names state the mechanism (`test_a_session_host_reads_the_stations_live_work`, `test_a_session_host_reloads_onto_current_code`), with no plan labels, stage names, ticket numbers or changelog prose.",
    "reasoning": "a finding \u2014 s117's stated base cost does not match the record the tree carries, and s118's premise contradicts the plan's own \u00a77.",
    "single_goal": "pass \u2014 s117 delivers one reading source the host answers from; s118 delivers one re-execution at an idle tick. Each has one gate.",
    "wiring": "pass \u2014 s117 and s118 declare no `plan-section-depends-on` entry, but the two up-streams they consume are already landed (s10's station live-work reading, declared done; the station reload of \u00a77/s7, done), so no gate is owed and no declared relationship points at a finding. The omission is a convention gap, not a wrong edge."
  },
